life is a mess there are all kinds of  forms of life on this planet and anytime  you want to do anything scientific it's  good to have some kind of organizing  principle biologists use a very rough  organizing principle for defining types  of life by calling them species species  traditionally was the distinction of  different animals or different forms of  life which cannot interbreed or even if  they do interbreed their offspring  cannot reproduce this is a rough  definition of course but it was useful  in categorizing and and enumerated the  number of types of forms of life on  Earth there are and now that that list  is in the millions we have a very  complicated web of what the Tree of Life  looks like but even more interesting is  that the ability to access the genetic  information of different species had  allowed biologists to see where the  lines are blurred between two different  types or more species what they found  was interesting first that species there  are many species which inner breed they  have sex with each other and they  produce offspring and a lot of genetic  information is shared between species  but what they've also found is that  their genetic distinguishing features  that remain robust it's like if you have  two cans of paint and you pour them into  each other say one yellow and one red  and you mix it all up and it all turns  orange except for these spots some are  exactly red and the other ones are  yellow and they don't blend for some  reason parts of the DNA which stay  robustly distinct between two species  one example is in northern Europe there  are two different species of crows the  carrion  and the hooded crow and yet they do in  her breed and they do live  geographically in overlapping places and  yet their distinguishing features remain  in fact their genetic codes are so  similar that you looking at the DNA  would never call them different species  and yet they look completely different  and therefore are easily distinguished  and the question is why why is it so  robust and we don't know and so studying  the genomes and great details of  neighboring species and lots of  different species we can understand what  we mean by the word species at all
 

